  "guide.bcrypt.title": "Bcrypt Hash / Verify Guide",
  "guide.bcrypt.desc": "Bcrypt guide: generate and verify password hashes with an adjustable cost factor, computed locally for safe storage.",
  "guide.bcrypt.intro": "Bcrypt is the go-to password hashing algorithm: it bakes in a salt so the same password yields different hashes each time. This tool generates hashes and verifies plaintext, with an adjustable cost factor (rounds), all in your browser.",
  "guide.bcrypt.features.0": "Standard Bcrypt hash ($2a$10$..., 60 chars)",
  "guide.bcrypt.features.1": "Built-in salt; same plaintext -> different hash each time",
  "guide.bcrypt.features.2": "Cost factor 8-14 to balance security and speed",
  "guide.bcrypt.features.3": "One-click verify plaintext + hash",
  "guide.bcrypt.features.4": "Auto-extract salt from the hash, no manual management",
  "guide.bcrypt.scenarios.0": "Debug user password hashes in backend dev",
  "guide.bcrypt.scenarios.1": "Learn/demo how Bcrypt works",
  "guide.bcrypt.scenarios.2": "Verify a password hash from your database",
  "guide.bcrypt.steps.0": "Enter the plaintext password",
  "guide.bcrypt.steps.1": "Pick a cost factor (10 recommended)",
  "guide.bcrypt.steps.2": "Click Generate Hash for a 60-char hash",
  "guide.bcrypt.steps.3": "Paste the hash into verify, enter plaintext, click Verify",
  "guide.bcrypt.tips.0": "Each +2 in cost factor ~= 4x slower; 10 is ~150ms",
  "guide.bcrypt.tips.1": "Bcrypt is hashing, not encryption - it cannot be reversed, only verified",
  "guide.bcrypt.tips.2": "Store the cost factor in config so you can upgrade later",
  "guide.bcrypt.faqs.0.q": "Why are two hashes different?",
  "guide.bcrypt.faqs.0.a": "Bcrypt salts randomly each time and writes the salt into the hash prefix, so results differ but all verify.",
  "guide.bcrypt.faqs.1.q": "Is a leaked hash safe?",
  "guide.bcrypt.faqs.1.a": "With a strong password it is relatively safe, but add a pepper or MFA.",
